# A histogram of samples: bin= on a number line stacks each bin's samples into a column; new ones drop in.
title "Sums of three dice"
schema numberline prop=total range=[3,18] bin=1
mark s0 dot roll total=6
mark s1 dot roll total=14
mark s2 dot roll total=4
mark s3 dot roll total=10
mark s4 dot roll total=6
mark s5 dot roll total=13
mark s6 dot roll total=6
mark s7 dot roll total=6
mark s8 dot roll total=12
mark s9 dot roll total=7
mark s10 dot roll total=15
mark s11 dot roll total=9
mark s12 dot roll total=13
mark s13 dot roll total=9
mark s14 dot roll total=9
mark s15 dot roll total=9
mark s16 dot roll total=9
mark s17 dot roll total=14
mark s18 dot roll total=10
mark s19 dot roll total=12
Say: "Roll three dice twenty times and stack each total."
mark s20 dot roll total=8
mark s21 dot roll total=7
mark s22 dot roll total=6
mark s23 dot roll total=14
mark s24 dot roll total=15
mark s25 dot roll total=11
mark s26 dot roll total=9
mark s27 dot roll total=12
mark s28 dot roll total=13
mark s29 dot roll total=9
mark s30 dot roll total=14
mark s31 dot roll total=13
mark s32 dot roll total=5
mark s33 dot roll total=11
mark s34 dot roll total=12
mark s35 dot roll total=6
mark s36 dot roll total=8
mark s37 dot roll total=10
mark s38 dot roll total=10
mark s39 dot roll total=10
mark s40 dot roll total=9
mark s41 dot roll total=12
mark s42 dot roll total=12
mark s43 dot roll total=10
mark s44 dot roll total=9
mark s45 dot roll total=12
mark s46 dot roll total=10
mark s47 dot roll total=5
mark s48 dot roll total=9
mark s49 dot roll total=11
mark s50 dot roll total=7
mark s51 dot roll total=7
mark s52 dot roll total=3
mark s53 dot roll total=13
mark s54 dot roll total=13
mark s55 dot roll total=10
mark s56 dot roll total=10
mark s57 dot roll total=7
mark s58 dot roll total=13
mark s59 dot roll total=8
Say: "Forty more, and the middle starts to |rise|rise."
@rise indicate s0
